lay down and slept; I awaked; for the Lord will help me.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":6,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"I will not be afraid of ten thousands of people, who beset me round about.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":7,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Arise, Lord; deliver me, my God: for you have struck all who were without cause my enemies; you have broken the teeth of sinners.","poem":1}]},{"type":"verse","number":8,"content":[{"lineBreak":true},{"text":"Deliverance is the Lord's, and your blessing is upon your people.","poem":1}]}],"footnotes":[{"noteId":5,"caller":"+","text":"The word Διάψαλμα (Selah) has been rendered Pause, as most intelligible to the English reader.","reference":{"chapter":3,"verse":2}}]},"thisChapterLink":"/api/eng_lxu/PSA/3.json","thisChapterAudioLinks":{},"nextChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_lxu/PSA/4.json","nextChapterAudioLinks":{},"previousChapterApiLink":"/api/eng_lxu/PSA/2.json","previousChapterAudioLinks":{},"numberOfVerses":8}